  "markdown": "London\n\n# Mercedes-AMG showroom, London\n\nSupply and fit of black matt Muraspec wallcoverings through one of the newest Mercedes showrooms in London, finished with brushed stainless-steel trims at the doors and skirtings.\n\n![Curved staircase beside walls finished in black matt wallcovering, Mercedes-AMG showroom, London.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/mercedes-amg-06-800.webp)\n\n## Project record\n\nClient, materials & project facts\n\n**Client**\n: A Mercedes-AMG showroom\n\n**Designer**\n: –Not recorded\n\n**Main contractor**\n: –Not recorded\n\n**Maker and paper**\n: Muraspec\n\n**Area or rooms**\n: –Not recorded\n\n**Scope**\n: Supply and installation of black matt wallcoverings\n\n**Year**\n: 2019\n\nIn September 2019 we supplied and fitted black matt Muraspec wallcoverings at one of the newest Mercedes showrooms in London, the AMG showroom photographed here. Black matt is the least forgiving finish there is: it shows every joint, every mark and every uneven wall under showroom lighting.\n\n## At a glance\n\n- **Where:** a Mercedes-AMG showroom in London\n- **When:** September 2019\n- **Scope:** supply and installation of black matt wallcoverings\n- **Wallcovering:** Muraspec, black matt\n- **Detail:** brushed stainless-steel trims around the doors and above the skirtings\n\n## Black matt\n\nOn a dark matt finish the joints are invisible only if the walls beneath are flat and the edges are cut clean, so the preparation decides the result. Hands, paste and tools are kept off the face of the material, because a mark on black matt cannot be wiped away.\n\n## The trims\n\nAround each door and above each skirting a narrow brushed stainless-steel trim finishes the edge of the wallcovering. The wallcovering is cut to meet the trim on one continuous line, so the steel reads as a deliberate frame rather than a cover strip.\n\n## Photographs on this page\n\nOur own photographs, first posted on our Instagram, [@mrwallcover](https://www.instagram.com/mrwallcover/), in September 2019 and May 2021: the finished showroom first, then the door and skirting details, and a collage from the works. The scope is recorded in our posts of 7 September 2019 ([see the post](https://www.instagram.com/p/B2HM9AWlG3w/)) and 13 September 2019 ([see the post](https://www.instagram.com/p/B2V9cZklfv9/)).\n\n## Photographs\n\n![Mercedes-AMG showroom entrance, London, with illuminated AMG branding against the black matt walls.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/mercedes-amg-05-800.webp)\n\n![Corridor of black matt wallcovering with steel-trimmed doors and skirting, Mercedes-AMG showroom, London.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/mercedes-amg-04-800.webp)\n\n![Black matt Muraspec walls around a door with a brushed stainless-steel trim, Mercedes-AMG showroom, London.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/mercedes-amg-02-800.webp)\n\n![Two doors set in black matt wallcovering with narrow brushed-steel trims, Mercedes-AMG showroom, London.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/mercedes-amg-03-800.webp)\n\n![Collage from the works at the Mercedes-AMG showroom, London: black matt walls, AMG signage and our installers at work.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/mercedes-amg-01-800.webp)\n\nHow the commission ran\n\n## The same standards, on every commission.\n\nEach commission has a written scope by room, walls prepared until they are true, protected floors, batch and shade control, set-out from the room’s focal points, and a return visit. [Read the method](https://www.mrwallcover.com/practice/#method).\n\nThe six standards in full\n\n01\n\n### Survey and scope, room by room\n\nWe measure the wall that will actually be hung, allow for the repeat and the wastage, and write a scope of works room by room before anyone orders paper.\n\n02\n\n### Preparation decides the finish\n\nWalls are filled, made good and primed until they are true. If a wall is not ready for the material specified, we say so before the last drop is ordered.\n\n03\n\n### Protection and containment\n\nFloors, furniture and finished joinery are protected as part of the hang. Work is contained and the place is left tidy each evening. In a home we are visitors; in a hotel we work around the house.\n\n04\n\n### Batch and shade control\n\nDeliveries are checked against the measure, and batches and shading are managed so that a corridor of rooms reads as one surface.\n\n05\n\n### Set out from the room's focal points\n\nPattern is set out from chimneypieces, doorcases and bed walls, so the pattern sits square to the cornice and the joinery.\n\n06\n\n### One team, then the return visit\n\nThe people who start are the people who finish. Four to six weeks after completion we come back to look at every seam and edge, and the workmanship is guaranteed for twelve months.\n\n[See the finish up close: seams, internal corners, edges and joins from our own installations](https://www.mrwallcover.com/details/)\n\nBy [Dorin Burcus](https://www.mrwallcover.com/about/#dorin), founder · Last updated 22 October 2026\n",
